Images with unknown usage terms
-------------------------------
The repository contains test and record images made with an image generator
(Codex imagegen) whose model and output usage terms are recorded as "unknown":
  - tests/pipeline/corpus/generated/ (16 calibration images; prompts, dates and
    SHA-256 in its README.md and manifest.json), and
  - e2e-tests/07-ds-turnaround/ (generated design originals, and the review
    sheets, stage images and exports that show or derive from them; provenance
    in each project's source/manifest.json and RECORD.md).
These images are not offered under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and no
license is claimed for them. They are excluded from the wheel and the sdist.
The generator's terms as understood are recorded in third_party/THIRD_PARTY.md
(L-12). The source records of the e2e-tests/03 and 04 round-trip projects say
"unknown" only because the import default was used; those images were drawn in
this project and are covered by Apache-2.0 like the rest of the repository.

Algorithm references
--------------------
The fixed-point colour distance specified in docs/SPEC.md (Appendix B) uses the
coefficients of the Oklab colour space published by Björn Ottosson.
Source: https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/
The author releases that code to the public domain, with MIT as an alternative.
CyberSprite uses the public-domain coefficients in its independently implemented
integer conversion; the normative coefficients are in docs/SPEC.md, Appendix B.
Platform identifiers describe technical compatibility only. DMG and NDS-class
presets are independent implementations and do not imply endorsement by Nintendo
or other trademark owners. All trademarks belong to their respective owners.
The authored gray-4 palette uses conventional shades, not standardized hardware RGB.
